namespace LingGuangV05.CaseMenu
{
    // Modern explanatory copy for the human player. Never feed this into character knowledge.
    public static partial class PlayerKnowledgeCopy
    {
        public static string Audience(bool english) => english ? "For the player" : "给屏幕前玩家的说明";
        public static string Context(bool english) => english
            ? "Modern explanations of AI and this game. These are not documents from the 2016 story world, and reading them does not give characters this knowledge."
            : "这是面向屏幕前玩家的现代 AI 与游戏说明，不是故事中 2016 年的资料；阅读不会让角色获知这些内容。";
        public static string Title1(bool english) => english ? "How are chatting and training different?" : "聊天和训练，有什么不同？";
        public static string Body1(bool english) => english ? "When you chat with an AI, it usually uses capabilities it has already learned, together with the current conversation, to generate a reply. Remembering your name or accepting a correction does not necessarily mean its internal parameters have changed.\n\nActual model training requires turning material or feedback into training data, then computing errors, backpropagating them and updating parameters to change how the model handles problems. Its results need to be checked with independent tests.\n\nConversations can become training material, but that requires additional data processing and a training process. Saving records, collecting feedback and completing training are different things.\n\nThis game turns that long, complex process into a playable experience of teaching and growth. Your teaching affects abilities, memory and conversation within the game. It does not mean that you are training a large language model from scratch on your computer, or that every chat changes the weights of the built-in local language model." : "当你与 AI 对话时，它通常是在利用已经学到的能力，结合当前聊天内容生成回答。它记住你的名字、接受一次纠正，并不一定意味着模型内部的参数发生了变化。\n\n真正的模型训练，需要把资料或反馈整理成训练数据，通过计算误差、反向传播和参数更新，让模型逐渐改变处理问题的方式，并用独立测试确认效果。\n\n对话也可以成为训练材料，但需要额外的数据处理和训练过程。保存了记录、收集了反馈、完成了训练，是不同的事情。\n\n本作将这个漫长而复杂的过程转化为可体验的培养玩法。玩家的教学会影响游戏中的能力成长、记忆与交流，但这不等于在自己的电脑上从零训练一个大语言模型，也不等于每次聊天都会修改内置本地语言模型的权重。";
        public static string Title2(bool english) => english ? "How smart must an AI be to count as a large language model?" : "AI 要多聪明，才算大语言模型？";
        public static string Body2(bool english) => english ? "A large language model is not a title an AI earns by reaching a certain level of intelligence.\n\nLanguage models mainly learn patterns in language sequences to predict or generate content. “Large” usually refers to model parameters and the scale of training, but there is no single dividing line that applies across all eras and research fields.\n\nFluent conversation does not prove that a model is large. Being good at chess or Go does not make it a language model. Large language models can also get calculations wrong, invent facts or fail in unfamiliar situations.\n\nTo judge what a model is, look at its type and how it was trained. To judge what it can do, look at specific tasks and independent tests. A model's name cannot substitute for evidence of its capabilities.\n\nThe growth stages in this game serve its gameplay and story. They are not a universal real-world technical path for turning a small program into a large language model." : "大语言模型不是 AI 达到某个智力等级后获得的称号。\n\n语言模型主要学习语言序列的规律，用于预测或生成内容；“大”通常涉及模型参数与训练规模，但没有适用于所有时代和研究领域的统一分界线。\n\n能流畅聊天，不足以证明模型规模很大；擅长下棋，也不意味着它是语言模型。大语言模型同样可能算错题、编造事实，或在陌生情境下失败。\n\n判断它是什么，需要看模型类型与训练方式；判断它能做什么，需要看具体任务和独立测试。模型的名字不能代替能力证明。\n\n本作的成长阶段服务于玩法与叙事，不是现实中“小程序升级成大语言模型”的统一技术路线。";
        public static string Title3(bool english) => english ? "Why can training require many GPUs?" : "为什么训练需要很多显卡？";
        public static string Body3(bool english) => english ? "Training requires more than storing the model. It also involves computing and storing parameter gradients, optimizer states and intermediate results needed for backpropagation. GPUs are good at processing the many matrix operations in a model in parallel. Multiple GPUs can share computation and storage and shorten training time.\n\nLarge-scale pretraining may need huge computing clusters, but training a small model or fine-tuning only some parameters may not. “Training a frontier model can require many GPUs” does not mean “all training requires many GPUs.” The file size of a quantized model also does not represent its memory requirements during training." : "训练不仅需要保存模型，还需要计算和保存参数梯度、优化器状态以及用于反向传播的中间结果。显卡擅长并行处理模型中的大量矩阵运算；多张显卡可以分担计算和存储，并缩短训练时间。\n\n大规模预训练可能需要庞大的计算集群，但小模型训练或部分参数微调未必如此。不能把“训练前沿大模型需要很多显卡”写成“所有训练都必须使用大量显卡”。量化后的模型文件大小，也不能代表训练时的内存需求。";
    }
}
